                <pb facs="0821" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6351 Bethlehem Steel Company/4:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-02T16:00:00-00:44">September 2, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Bethlehem Steel asks Liberian Government for geological survey and expresses
                    interest in future exploitation of the country’s iron ore. President will inform
                    corporation that arrangements have already been effected to make a survey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
